    "question": "What SPF sunscreen do I actually need, and does a higher number meaningfully protect me more?",
    "summary": "SPF measures how much UVB radiation a sunscreen blocks, with SPF 30 blocking 97% and SPF 50 blocking 98% — a small but practically meaningful difference due to real-world under-application. Dermatologists recommend at least SPF 30 for daily use, broad-spectrum coverage for UVA protection, and…",
